From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HFM <hfm@example.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:41:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] subsys/pmci/mctp: add DSP0236 control responder; wire
 Type 2 into serial_bridge

Add the baseline MCTP control-protocol responder needed for a bus owner
(OpenBMC's mctpd) to enumerate a statically-addressed endpoint, and wire
the Type 2 sensor into the serial_bridge sample so pldmd can discover and
poll it end to end.

Key pieces:

  * include/zephyr/pmci/mctp/mctp_control.h + subsys/pmci/mctp/mctp_control.c
    (CONFIG_MCTP_CONTROL) - control responder.
      libmctp only routes transport-specific control commands (0xF0-0xFF)
      to a binding; the baseline commands land on the generic message
      handler. This responder installs itself as the MCTP rx_all callback,
      answers Set/Get Endpoint ID (0x01/0x02), Get MCTP Version Support
      (0x04) and Get Message Type Support (0x05) - reporting message types
      {0x00 control, 0x01 PLDM} - and forwards every non-control message to
      the downstream handler (the PLDM dispatcher) it was chained onto.
      Wire formats match mctpd's strict validation (IID echo, exact
      response length). The node keeps its fixed EID 18, so Set Endpoint ID
      accepts only a matching or no-change (0) request.

  * samples/.../serial_bridge - integration.
      Enable CONFIG_MCTP_CONTROL + CONFIG_PLDM_TYPE_PLATFORM; register a
      simulated die-temperature Numeric Sensor (sensor_id 1) with the Type 2
      responder; chain the control responder above the PLDM dispatcher. Also
      adds a reverse-direction probe thread that queries the BMC (EID 8) with
      GetTID/GetPLDMTypes/GetPLDMVersion to exercise the host->BMC path.

With this, mctpd runs Get Endpoint ID / Get Message Type Support against
the node, publishes it on D-Bus, and pldmd's platform-mc discovers it and
polls GetSensorReading. The BMC-side enablement is patch 0006.

Signed-off-by: HFM <hfm@example.com>
